 "kind": "definition",
 "title": "Finite-degree data attached to a closed center in Proj",
 "statement": "Let $\\mathcal I$ be a finite type quasi-coherent ideal on a qcqs scheme\n$X$, let $\\mathcal A=\\bigoplus_{n\\geq0}\\mathcal I^n$, let\n$X'=\\operatorname{Proj}_X(\\mathcal A)$, and let\n$Z'\\hookrightarrow X'$ be of finite presentation. Select, by classical\nchoice from the nonempty witness type supplied by\n[lemma-nagata-proj-closed-center-finite-degree-exists], a pair\n$(d,\\mathcal F)$. No property of the selected pair is built into this\ndefinition. Denote it by\n$\\mathsf{FD}(Z')=(d(Z'),\\mathcal F(Z'))$.",
 "source": {
  "document": "literature/blueprint/master/blueprint/sec-nagata-compactification/sk-lem-nagata-sketch-blowups/def-nagata-proj-closed-center-finite-degree.md",
  "place": "node def-nagata-proj-closed-center-finite-degree, order 130"
 },
 "stmt_deps": [
  "lemma-nagata-proj-closed-center-finite-degree-exists"
 ],
 "proof": [
  {
   "text": "## Properties of the finite-degree center data\n\nThe selected integer $d(Z')$ is positive, $\\mathcal F(Z')$ is a finite\ntype submodule of $\\mathcal I^{d(Z')}$, and\n\n$$\nZ'=\\operatorname{Proj}_X\n\\bigl(\\mathcal A/\\mathcal F(Z')\\mathcal A\\bigr).\n$$\n\nMoreover the support of\n$\\mathcal I^{d(Z')}/\\mathcal F(Z')$ lies over the underlying topological\nimage $b(|Z'|)$ together with the first center.",
   "uses": [],
   "elementary": null
  },
  {
   "text": "*Proof.*\nThese are the properties required of the witness selected in\n[def-nagata-proj-closed-center-finite-degree]; existence of such a\nwitness is\n[lemma-nagata-proj-closed-center-finite-degree-exists].",
   "uses": [
    "lemma-nagata-proj-closed-center-finite-degree-exists"
   ],
   "elementary": false
  }
 ],
